The USCIS work gets a place in the sidebar

"i don't see the UCSIS form in the web." (JJ, 2026-10-09) It was all
there -- the G-28, the twelve combo packages, the edition tracker, the
Federal Register watch -- and all of it was reachable only from inside a
client profile. There was no nav entry, so from the front of the app none
of it existed. A feature nobody can find is a feature nobody has.

/admin/uscis lists the twenty tracked forms by practice area with the
edition read off each PDF, every combo package with its one-line shape,
and, in red at the top, anything to look at before filing: today that is
the G-28, whose OMB control number lapsed on 05/31/2021 on the copy USCIS
serves at its own address.

It does not pretend a form can be filled from nowhere. A G-28 is about a
particular person, so the page sends you to the client list and the
filling happens from their file, where the prefill has something to read.

The page says when the editions were last read. A page of edition numbers
with no date on it is one that gets trusted long after it stops being
true, so check-uscis-packages.js asserts the date is on it.

